<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Shutdown (255)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>shutdown
</pre>
<p>Stops the game at once, without a countdown: every player is told 
"Shutdown by &lt;your name&gt;.", is saved, and the server exits. Type the 
command in full; an abbreviation is refused.
</p><p>Note that whatever keeps the game running on the server (the runvme.sh 
script, or a system service) usually starts it again whenever it exits, 
so on such a server shutdown works like an unannounced reboot. To keep 
the game down, stop that on the server itself. To restart with a warning 
to the players, use <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Crash</a>
</pre>




</div>